   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "faq",
     "kind": "nested-accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "Understanding the 28-Gram Daily Limit",
       "open": true,
       "blocks": [
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": 4,
         "text": "Understanding the 28-Gram Daily Limit",
         "dev": [
          "tablet",
          "mobile_extra",
          "mobile"
         ]
        },
        {
         "t": "rich",
         "html": "<p>The state allows you to purchase <b>28 grams of flower or its equivalent</b> in other cannabis formats. Let’s break down how these limits apply:</p><p>• <b>Flower</b>: Up to <b>28 grams</b> (1 ounce).</p><p>• <b>Edibles</b>: A total of <b>500mg THC</b>, which is roughly <b>5 packs of 20 servings</b>, each serving containing <b>5mg of THC</b>.</p><p>• <b>Concentrates</b>: Up to <b>5 grams</b> of cannabis concentrates, such as wax, shatter, or live resin (equivalent to <b>5 x 1g</b> or <b>10 x 0.5g</b> packages).</p><p>• <b>Tinctures</b>: A total of <strong>5000mg</strong> = approximately <strong>5</strong><b> x 1000mg bottles</b>, depending on the product’s potency and total THC content.</p><p>• <b>Pre-roll Joints</b>: <b>28 pre-roll joints</b>, assuming each joint contains roughly <b>1 gram of flower</b>.</p><p>• <b>Vape Cartridges</b>: Up to <b>10 x 0.5g cartridges</b> or <b>5 x 1g cartridges/disposables</b>.</p>",
         "dev": [
          "tablet",
          "mobile_extra",
          "mobile"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "q": "Why Are Purchase Limits Important?",
       "blocks": [
        {
         "t": "rich",
         "html": "<p>Massachusetts’ purchase limits serve three critical purposes:</p><p><b>• Encourage Responsible Use</b>: Limiting daily purchases helps consumers manage their intake responsibly.</p><p><b>• Prevent Diversion</b>: Restricting quantities reduces the risk of products entering the illicit market.</p><p><b>• Promote Safety</b>: Regulating how much THC a consumer can access in one day helps prevent overconsumption.</p>",
         "dev": [
          "tablet",
          "mobile_extra",
          "mobile"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "q": "Tips for Staying Within the Limit",
       "blocks": [
        {
         "t": "rich",
         "html": "<p>• <b>Know Your Preferences</b>: Decide what products suit your needs—flower, concentrates, edibles, or a mix.</p><p>• <b>Plan Ahead</b>: If you intend to purchase multiple product types, calculate the total equivalency before checkout.</p><p>• <b>Consult the Experts</b>: Dispensary staff can help you understand product potencies and their impact on the daily limit.</p>",
         "dev": [
          "tablet",
          "mobile_extra",
          "mobile"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
